# Omarchy-Jezzball — example Hyprland configuration
#
# How to use it: copy whichever lines you want into your
# `~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf` (or `source = ~/.config/hypr/jezzball.conf`
# pointing at this file).
# Syntax valid for recent Hyprland releases (windowrulev2 + bind).
#
# The window class is `omarchy-jezzball` (contract §14:
# StartupWMClass=omarchy-jezzball). If a rule does not seem to apply, check the
# real class with `hyprctl clients | grep -A2 jezzball`.

# --- Window: floating, initial size 1280x800, centred ---
# `float` keeps the game from reshuffling your tiles when it opens.
windowrulev2 = float, class:^(omarchy-jezzball)$
# A sensible initial size for a 64x40 cell arena plus the HUD.
windowrulev2 = size 1280 800, class:^(omarchy-jezzball)$
# Centred on open.
windowrulev2 = center, class:^(omarchy-jezzball)$

# --- Optional (uncomment if you want them) ---
# Lock the size so the mouse maps 1:1 onto the arena:
# windowrulev2 = minsize 960 600, class:^(omarchy-jezzball)$
# windowrulev2 = maxsize 1600 1000, class:^(omarchy-jezzball)$
# Drop the border/decoration if you prefer a clean in-game look:
# windowrulev2 = noborder, class:^(omarchy-jezzball)$

# --- Example keybind: SUPER+J launches the game ---
# Change the key to whatever you prefer. `exec` launches it in the background.
bind = SUPER, J, exec, omarchy-jezzball
# Variant: open straight into a specific mode (requires the app to accept
# `--mode`, see packaging/omarchy-jezzball.desktop):
# bind = SUPER_SHIFT, J, exec, omarchy-jezzball --mode enhanced
